{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  ak-archive-magazine.liquid  —  "AmeriKid Archive" magazine
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A self-contained, tactile printed-zine magazine that replaces the cassette
  deck on the /collections (list-collections) Archive page. Rough printed
  archive object (halftone/grain/physical paper) — NOT a flat flipbook, NOT
  an 8-bit game UI.

  STATES (class on .ak-mag root): is-closed -> is-opening -> is-open
    - is-closed : an angled, dimensional closed cover resting on the paper,
                  idle float + interactive hover (tilt/lift/shadow). Cover
                  title = "ARCHIVE". Click/Enter to open.
    - is-opening: book squares-up toward the viewer, the cover swings open
                  (delayed) and fades; the centred spread is revealed. NO
                  lateral slide (the book never translates horizontally).
    - is-open   : centred two-page spread (desktop) / single page (mobile);
                  prev/next + "Close Issue" below the book; clean readable pages.

  - Self-contained: all HTML + CSS + JS inline. No external dep / canvas / WebGL
    / new font (reuses ak-due-date.woff2 + ak-tenada.woff2 assets).
  - Reuses the notebook paper from snippets/ak-notebook-archive (custom_liquid_akArch1).
  - Logo: reuses settings.logo (same header/nav logo), never a hardcoded URL.

  INTERIOR BACKGROUND ART:
    --ak-mag-bg below points at an owner-supplied Shopify Files image used as a
    low-opacity printed collage texture INSIDE the pages (never the cover). Each
    page uses a different background-position (see BGPOS in the JS) so pages
    don't look identical. To swap it, change the --ak-mag-bg URL only.

  FUTURE COVER ART HOOK:
    The closed cover is a clean typographic cover by design. To drop in real
    cover art later: add an image_picker setting (e.g. "cover_image") to
    {% schema %} and render it into `.ak-mag-cover-art` (placeholder span
    already in the markup), or set --ak-mag-cover-image on `.ak-mag-cover-face`.
    Do NOT hardcode a CDN asset for the cover.

  REVERT (whole magazine): in templates/list-collections.json remove
  "ak-archive-magazine" from `order`, set "ak-archive" "disabled": false — the
  byte-frozen cassette deck returns identical. Then delete this file.
  sections/ak-archive.liquid is NEVER edited either way.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  ===== ARCHIVE DATA (18 items, in display order) =================================
  HOW TO ADD ANOTHER ARCHIVE ITEM LATER (keep this simple — three aligned lists):
    1. Append the item TITLE to `mag_titles` (use "|" as the separator).
    2. Append its collection URL to `mag_urls` at the SAME position.
    3. Append its image filename (uploaded in Shopify > Content > Files) to
       `mag_imgs` at the SAME position.
    4. All three lists MUST stay the same length and the SAME order — index N in
       each list describes one item. No other change is needed; the masthead,
       contents index, page count, and counters all derive from these lists.
  (Titles must not contain a "|". Order here = the order shown in the issue.)
  ================================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
